<%- include('partials/header') %>

<div style="max-width:720px;margin:0 auto">

  <div class="module">
    <h2>What happens to what you put here</h2>
    <div class="body">
      <p style="margin-top:0">
        This page is meant to be accurate rather than reassuring. Where something
        is not protected, it says so.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="module">
    <div class="modhead">Your photos</div>
    <div class="body">
      <p style="margin-top:0"><b>Nothing here is reachable from the open internet.</b>
      There is no sign-up page and no way to find this site. Every page requires a
      login, and photo files return "not found" to anyone without one. Search
      engines and scrapers never see it, because they cannot get past the door.</p>

      <p><b>Location data is removed before your photo is stored.</b> A picture
      taken on a phone normally carries GPS coordinates accurate to a few metres,
      your device model, and the exact time. Upload a photo taken at home and that
      file would otherwise tell people where you live. We strip all of it the
      moment the file arrives &mdash; the picture is kept, everything hidden
      inside it is discarded.</p>

      <p><b>No third party ever sees anything.</b> There are no adverts, no
      analytics, no tracking scripts, no fonts or images loaded from other
      companies' servers. Nobody can embed an image from elsewhere, so no outside
      site can learn that you viewed a page. Your pictures are not used to train
      anything, sold, or shared, because they never leave this server.</p>

      <p class="dim"><b>What we cannot do:</b> stop another member taking a
      screenshot. Once a person can see a picture, they can keep it. No app has
      ever solved this, and anything that claims to is pretending. The real
      protection is that everyone here was invited by someone who vouched for
      them &mdash; so invite accordingly.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="module">
    <div class="modhead">Your messages</div>
    <div class="body">
      <p style="margin-top:0">Messages and chats are private between the people in
      them. No other member can read them.</p>
      <p><b>They are not end-to-end encrypted.</b> They are stored on the server as
      ordinary text, which means whoever administers this site
      <% if (typeof tom !== 'undefined' && tom) { %>(<a href="/u/<%= tom.username %>"><%= tom.display_name %></a>)<% } %>
      is technically able to read them. They have no reason to and would have to
      go out of their way, but you should know it is possible rather than assume
      otherwise. If that matters for a particular conversation, have it somewhere
      built for that.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="module">
    <div class="modhead">Where it all lives</div>
    <div class="body">
      <p style="margin-top:0">One server, rented from a hosting company, with the
      disk encrypted. Everything &mdash; accounts, messages, photos, songs &mdash;
      sits in a single file and a single folder on that disk. No other company is
      involved and nothing is copied anywhere else, except backups the
      administrator keeps so a hardware failure doesn't erase everyone's history.</p>
      <p>Connections are encrypted in transit. Passwords are stored scrambled in a
      way that cannot be reversed, so even someone holding the database cannot
      read them.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="module">
    <div class="modhead">Leaving</div>
    <div class="body">
      <p style="margin-top:0">You can delete your account yourself at any time from
      <a href="/settings">Settings</a>. It removes your profile, photos, posts,
      comments and messages. Two honest caveats: anything another member already
      saved or screenshotted is beyond our reach, and backups taken before you left
      will still contain your data until they age out.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="module">
    <div class="modhead">In one line</div>
    <div class="body">
      <p style="margin-top:0;font-size:17px;font-family:var(--serif)">
        Nobody outside can get in. Nothing is sold, scraped or used to train
        anything. Your photos carry no hidden location. The people who can see
        your things are the people you can see &mdash; and the person running the
        server.
      </p>
      <p class="dim">Questions about any of this are fair game. Ask.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
